        "severity": "major",
        "evidence": "trace-locality-...-proof.md:46-65 — 'The product factorisation then follows from the multiplicativity of the standard trace on products of matrix units in distinct positions of the same block.' The standard trace is NOT multiplicative on products of matrix units (tr(E_ij E_kl)=δ_jk δ_il, and tr is linear not multiplicative); the claim that tr_M(NF(β)) equals a PRODUCT ∏_i V̂_i over normal-form generators does not follow from 'multiplicativity of the standard trace' (no such property). The mechanism by which a sum-over-blocks weighted trace becomes a single product over normal-form letters is not bridged — the key step (md:53-57) invokes a non-existent multiplicativity.",
        "notes": "Major logical gap: 'multiplicativity of the standard trace on products of matrix units' is false as stated; traces are not multiplicative. The product-factorisation bridge (the whole point of part 3) rests on this mis-stated property. Either a different mechanism (e.g. the trace being a single matrix-unit coefficient times a path weight that telescopes) must be supplied, or the step is a non-sequitur."
      }
